  },
  {
    question: 'How can I make my written communication clearer?',
    answer: '<p>Techniques for clearer writing:</p><ul><li><strong>Front-load the point:</strong> Key message in the first sentence</li><li><strong>Use structure:</strong> Bullet points, numbered lists, headers</li><li><strong>Define terms:</strong> Don\'t assume shared vocabulary</li><li><strong>Include context:</strong> Why you\'re asking, what you\'ll do with the answer</li><li><strong>State the ask explicitly:</strong> What you need, from whom, by when</li><li><strong>Read it aloud:</strong> Catches awkward phrasing and unclear sentences</li></ul>'
  },
  {
    question: 'What if someone consistently misunderstands me?',
    answer: '<p>Patterns suggest a systemic issue:</p><ul><li><strong>Check your communication:</strong> Are you being as clear as you think?</li><li><strong>Ask for feedback:</strong> "I notice we\'ve had some miscommunications—what could I do differently?"</li><li><strong>Try different formats:</strong> Maybe they process video better than text, or vice versa</li><li><strong>Document agreements:</strong> Written records of what was decided</li><li><strong>More frequent check-ins:</strong> Catch misalignments earlier</li></ul><p>Address patterns directly rather than letting frustration build.</p>'
  },
  {
    question: 'How do I communicate across cultural differences?',
    answer: '<p>Cultural differences affect communication styles:</p><ul><li><strong>Learn preferences:</strong> Some cultures are more direct, others more indirect</li><li><strong>Be explicit:</strong> Don\'t rely on hints or implications</li><li><strong>Confirm understanding:</strong> Especially for important messages</li><li><strong>Ask questions:</strong> "How would you prefer I communicate this?"</li><li><strong>Be patient:</strong> Non-native speakers may need more time</li></ul><p>When in doubt, over-communicate and verify understanding.</p>'
